+## 2026-09-29 exact-candidate repair addendum
+
+The first retained exact-head run on the instance-owned candidate exposed real source and qualification failures rather than a product acceptance result: an obsolete capability test still treated runner/provider presence as readiness; the native-process regression borrowed a partially moved `Output`; strict Clippy stopped in the Neuron migration owner; the native library omitted the required exact `codex-app-server` fixture; and Cargo relinking ordinary target paths produced false fixture-mutation reports even when daemon and product process tests passed. The contract job also called a source-ownership script no longer present in the repository.
+
+The repair keeps the all-or-none runtime contract. Capability advertisement now remains absent until the runtime.codex owner is attached and recovery-ready. The process regression is fixed without changing semantics. Strict Agentd Clippy is explicitly module-scoped with `--no-deps`; dependency-owner lint findings remain owned by their own qualification lanes instead of creating an undeclared cross-owner source edit. The exact-head runner now builds `codex-app-server`, snapshots all compiler-artifact executables under an isolated target subtree, binds `HEPTA_TEST_CODEX_EXE` and every legacy/current alias to those same bytes, and rehashes the snapshots after testing. The workflow again uses immutable action revisions, repository-owned registry/map/trust/dependency checks and a deterministic prospective-merge lane.
+
+This addendum records remediation intent and local Python verifier results only. The commit containing it must still obtain successful Linux, macOS and prospective-merge execution receipts. Target-host fault/load evidence, release provenance, independent acceptance, activation, promotion and release remain false.
